      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the feedback. I looked into this some more. Dispatching by `EventType` directly seems more straightforward than the alternative: `eventData[0]` comes straight from the FD and already tells you which ASIC sent the fault. I considered inferring the ASIC from `configPath` instead, so `RAINBOW_FAULT` and `ARKE_FAULT` could merge into one type. But that still needs some hardcoded way to recognize Rainbow vs Arke, just moved to a string match, and that signal seems less reliable than `eventData[0]`.",
